schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Regenerative Finance (ReFi)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    Tools and projects built to create economies that restore ecosystems and
    communities rather than deplete them; the article quotes Ethereum's own
    explainer describing ReFi as systems that "create value for participants
    while simultaneously benefiting ecosystems and communities."
  source_traditions:
    - Web3 / crypto-native regenerative-economics movement (ReFi DAO, Greenpill Network)
    - Ethereum Foundation's own ReFi explainer (ethereum.org/refi)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used as the umbrella "corner" of the crypto space this guide points
    newcomers toward, deliberately distinguished ("closer to compost than to
    a casino") from purely speculative crypto culture.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - Impact investing / ESG finance (non-crypto analogue, not discussed in article)
    - Regenerative agriculture / permaculture economics (the article's bridging analogy)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      ReFi (a values/mission orientation within web3) vs. crypto broadly
      (which includes purely speculative or extractive projects the article
      explicitly warns readers away from).
  tensions:
    - >-
      The "closer to compost than to a casino" framing is aspirational
      branding as much as description; the article does not examine whether
      self-labeled ReFi projects consistently deliver on that framing.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Presenting ReFi DAO and Greenpill as *the* two front doors risks implying
    ReFi is smaller/more centralized than the many overlapping, loosely
    connected circles the article itself says exist ("no single crypto
    community").
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/find-your-community.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
